        "done": true,
        "valid": true,
        "solids": 2,
        "signedVolume": 2000
      }
    },
    "comparison": {
      "equal": true,
      "differences": []
    },
    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides: done, valid, solid count and signedVolume of the boolean result (centred 10 mm cube fused with the 10 mm cube at origin (9.999,0,0), fuzzy 0.01). Bridge: Shape.fused(with:tolerance:) non-nil (OCCTShapeUnionEx returns nullptr when the BRepAlgoAPI operation is not done), isValid, subShapes(ofType: .solid).count and Shape.signedVolume, the raw BRepGProp mass, used instead of volume because Shape.volume is nil for an empty result. The test asserted non-nil and valid. Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse with SetArguments/SetTools and SetFuzzyValue(0.01), IsDone, BRepCheck_Analyzer, TopExp::MapShapes solid count, BRepGProp::VolumeProperties; fuseWithTolerance line of the transcript at %.17g. The cubes do not touch (the first spans x -5..5, the second starts at 9.999), so the result is two disjoint solids and the fuzzy value is never exercised. Doubles are compared to 1e-9 relative.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-tolerance/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  },
