    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantity on both sides: done, valid, solid count and signedVolume of the boolean result (centred 10 mm cube minus the 10 mm cube at origin (5,5,5), fuzzy 0.001). Bridge: Shape.subtracted(_:tolerance:) non-nil (OCCTShapeSubtractEx returns nullptr when the BRepAlgoAPI operation is not done), isValid, subShapes(ofType: .solid).count and Shape.signedVolume, the raw BRepGProp mass, used instead of volume because Shape.volume is nil for an empty result. The test asserted non-nil and valid. Kernel: BRepAlgoAPI_Cut with SetArguments/SetTools and SetFuzzyValue(0.001), IsDone, BRepCheck_Analyzer, TopExp::MapShapes solid count, BRepGProp::VolumeProperties; cutWithTolerance line of the transcript at %.17g. The cubes meet only at the corner (5,5,5), so the cut returns the first cube unchanged. Doubles are compared to 1e-9 relative.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-modeling-boolean-tolerance/probe-evidence-fix.mm (transcript-evidence-fix.txt)"
  },
